{title: 427 - No Night There}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Doctrines}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Fm]In the land [Ab7]of fadeless [Fm]day
[Ebm/Gb]Lies “the city [Db/F]foursquare;”
[Db/F]It shall never [Ab]pass [Eb7/G]away,
[Ebm/Gb]And there is [Db/F]“no night there.”

Refrain:
[Db]God [Fm]shall [Db/Ab]"wipe [Fm]away [Gb]all tears;"
[Ab7/Eb]There's no death, no [Db/Ab]pain, nor fears;
[Ab]And [Db/Ab]they count [Bbm]not time [Ebm/Bb]by [Ab7/Gb]years,
[Db/F]For there is [Ebm/Gb]"no night [Db/F]there."

Verse 2:
[Fm]All the gates [Ab7]of pearl [Eb7/G]are [Fm]made,
[Ebm/Gb]In "the city [Db/F]four-square;"
[Db/F]All the streets [Gm]with [Ab]gold [Eb7/G]are [Db]laid,
[Ebm/Gb]And there is [Db/F]"no night there."

Verse 3:
[Fm]And the gates [Ab7]shall never [Fm]close
[Ebm/Gb]To "the city [Db/F]four-square;"
[Db/F]There life's [Gm]crystal [Ab]river [Db]flows,
[Ebm/Gb]And there is [Db/F]"no night there."

Verse 4:
[Fm]There they need [Ab7]no sunshine [Fm]bright,
[Ebm/Gb]In "that city [Db/F]four-square;"
[Db/F]For the Lamb [Gm]is [Ab]all [Eb7/G]the [Db]light,
[Ebm/Gb]And there is [Db/F]"no night there."
